// The forward-vector, derived so that a world point at camPos + forward*d
// lands on the camera's -Z axis after view = rotate_y(-yaw)*translate(-cam)
// (see ../../../../gfx/frame.id and the README's derivation): forward =
// (-sin(yaw), -cos(yaw)). Scaled by move_speed() and divided back down so
// the result is a milli-unit step per key event.

fwd_dx() {
} return int (0 - sin_deg(ps_get(2))) * move_speed() / 1000;

fwd_dz() {
} return int (0 - cos_deg(ps_get(2))) * move_speed() / 1000;
